\subsubsection{Physical Conservation Metrics}

The ratio of generated to real energy and enstrophy fluctuates around $1.0$ throughout
training, indicating that the generator broadly preserves these integral invariants of
the 2D Navier--Stokes equations. However, the oscillatory behavior particularly in
enstrophy, which exhibits excursions between $0.78$ and $1.16$ suggests that the
physics discriminator provides a regularizing signal rather than enforcing strict
conservation.

The Navier--Stokes residual on the validation set increased from approximately $13$
at epoch 0 to values oscillating between $17$ and $20$ throughout the remainder of
training. The residual remains noisy and does not
 decrease. Which can suggest a flaw in conservation adjustments.

