promotes statistically consistent turbulent structures without enforcing them through
explicit equation constraints, and that the generator successfully approximates the
spectral properties of the ground-truth 2D turbulent fields across the resolved range
of scales.

\subsection{Super-Resolution}

A fundamental property of Fourier Neural Operators is their formulation directly
on function spaces, rendering the learned mapping independent of the discretization
grid used during training. To validate this in the context of turbulent vorticity
dynamics, a zero-shot super-resolution rollout was performed: the pretrained
generator was applied autoregressively to an initial condition upsampled from
$64{\times}64$ to $256{\times}256$ resolution,
$\omega_{\text{HR}}^0 \in \mathbb{R}^{256 \times 256} =
\operatorname{Interp}(\omega_{\text{LR}}^0)$, demonstrating the model's inherent
capability to operate on finer grids without retraining.

